==Japanese==
{{ja-kanjitab|ひだり|き|yomi=k}}

===Etymology===
/hidarikiki/: [pidarikiki] → [ɸidarikiki] → [çidarikiki]. Compound of {{compound|ja|左|tr1=hidari|t1=left|利き|tr2=kiki|t2=effective}}. See {{m|ja|左利き|tr=hidarigiki}}. For alternative pronunciation: /hidarigiki/: [pidarigiki] → [ɸidarigiki] → [çidarigiki]. Compound of {{compound|ja|左|tr1=hidari|t1=left|利き|tr2=kiki|t2=effective}}. /kiki/ voices to [giki] due to [[w:Rendaku|compounding]].

===Noun===
{{ja-noun|ひだりきき|ひだりぎき}}

# the ability to use a left hand better than a right hand; [[left-handedness]]
# a person who can use their left hand better than their right hand; [[left-handed]] [[person]]
#* {{RQ:Nippo Jisho|229}}
#*: '''Fidariguiqi'''. ヒダリギキ (左利き) 左利きの人.

